) Taiwan's Pingxi!

00:03:22.833 --> 00:03:27.066
Very waterfall,

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:52.466
Indonesian version! Feeling
up for an Indonesian climb?

00:03:52.466 --> 00:03:54.100
Go down to the bottom
of the waterfall.

00:03:54.866 --> 00:03:57.033
Wear your basis sandals now.

00:03:57.133 --> 00:03:59.000
(Wear sandals as you will be
treading water) All the way

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:14.066
down Usually this attraction
is in mainland China.

00:04:14.066 --> 00:04:15.900
There would be a cable car,

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:18.633
but this is Indonesia, so there isn't,
so you can take the cable car down.

00:04:21.733 --> 00:04:23.300
I've been waiting for
almost five minutes,

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:25.100
and they're still in the race.

00:04:27.133 --> 00:04:28.333
The reason for the racecars.
Down here,

00:04:32.866 --> 00:04:36.233
you can also take this waterway.

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:39.466
This side is all waterfalls

00:04:43.166 --> 00:04:44.700
Taroko Canyon (？？？？)

00:05:03.100 --> 00:05:07.400
Because the waterfalls are in the back,
all very much like in ....

00:05:10.833 --> 00:05:15.400
It's raining. I was just looking
at the waterfall from up there.

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:19.466
Let's wait, let's take a

00:05:20.533 --> 00:05:23.933
bridge and go swimming.

00:05:36.433 --> 00:05:38.033
Rainbow! Triathlon picker! Checking

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:42.066
out the terrain now!

00:05:42.066 --> 00:05:45.433
Where's the best place to go
for a swim? The return trip,

00:05:52.633 --> 00:05:56.533
it's a race to the top.

00:06:00.066 --> 00:06:02.100
Indonesia 101 Race

00:06:10.666 --> 00:06:12.666
Pineapple Durian

00:06:12.666 --> 00:06:16.400
It's kind of like sweet sugarcane.

00:06:16.900 --> 00:06:21.933
Snakeberries. Can we talk about this?

00:06:21.933 --> 00:06:25.133
You can pick up snakeberries on the road (there are many on the roadside,
you don't have to buy them).

00:06:30.633 --> 00:06:33.466
Ten thousand NT dollars
for a stretch of road,

00:06:36.100 --> 00:06:38.300
eighteen NT dollars from Shengguang
to the vegetable garden

00:06:40.533 --> 00:06:41.766
My little hands have nowhere to grab!

00:06:48.666 --> 00:06:50.933
I'm using all my abs right now!

00:06:54.233 --> 00:06:56.333
The vegetable garden is connected
to a convenient

00:07:00.633 --> 00:07:02.400
house! Now I'm leaning
forward completely.

00:07:10.333 --> 00:07:13.400
(Lunch was at a restaurant after the waterfall, which was quite Chinese
-style.)

00:07:16.500 --> 00:07:19.400
Is it spicy? (This is okay.
) (Not as spicy as yesterday.)

00:07:23.466 --> 00:07:25.000
You get a cute little flag (Why did

00:07:32.933 --> 00:07:36.000
I encounter a Pokémon
- Scorpion!)

00:07:40.233 --> 00:07:43.200
I almost threw up after
driving on a very

00:07:43.200 --> 00:07:46.266
bumpy mountain road
to the Bromo Hotel.

00:07:46.266 --> 00:07:49.566
And I have a slight headache. The
temperature is quite cold now,

00:07:49.566 --> 00:07:52.566
around ten degrees Celsius.

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:58.166
I felt too tired and the shaking was too much,
so I didn't eat.

00:07:58.166 --> 00:07:59.566
Motion sickness medication,

00:07:59.566 --> 00:08:02.766
and we're currently at an altitude of 2100 meters,
so we're being driven directly to 2100 meters.

00:08:02.766 --> 00:08:04.133
Bromo (I couldn't finish it,

00:08:07.600 --> 00:08:09.133
so I just ordered stir
-fried vegetables).

00:08:09.133 --> 00:08:11.633
Because we need to leave
very early tomorrow,

00:08:11.633 --> 00:08:15.366
around 2:00 AM, it should be...

00:08:15.366 --> 00:08:19.000
Climbing mountains in the dark is a bit
like climbing mountains in Taiwan.

00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:22.100
If all goes well,
we'll come back for breakfast.

00:08:23.866 --> 00:08:27.366
Songxuelou doesn't
have air conditioning,

00:08:31.866 --> 00:08:32.566
so it should have hot water.

00:08:35.366 --> 00:08:39.000
We need to take a jeep to
Bromo's viewpoint

00:08:39.600 --> 00:08:42.933
at 3 AM to secure a good spot.

00:08:42.933 --> 00:08:46.266
The room was very warm
and comfortable,

00:08:46.666 --> 00:08:48.866
pretty cool, and there was a Jeep.

00:08:48.866 --> 00:08:50.466
Super crowded

00:08:54.533 --> 00:08:57.366
looks

00:08:57.366 --> 00:08:59.566
What's wrong? You seem upset.

00:09:03.400 --> 00:09:06.400
(Everyone's so sleepy zzzzz)

00:09:15.966 --> 00:09:18.800
The scene of illegal parking in Wuling
XDDD Everyone parked on the highway

00:09:18.800 --> 00:09:21.000
Stop on the left and right,

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:24.366
line up in a row, basically cramming this side in. If you want to get up here,
this is...

00:09:24.366 --> 00:09:25.533
Jeep and horse

00:09:34.766 --> 00:09:36.233
roasting corn!

00:09:43.200 --> 00:09:45.466
We are currently at the observation

00:09:47.766 --> 00:09:48.966
deck; sunrise is at 5:30 AM.

00:09:48.966 --> 00:09:51.033
It's quite scary; there
are no railings here,

00:09:51.033 --> 00:09:53.600
so please be careful not to fall.
You can buy some hot food here.

00:09:53.600 --> 00:09:55.733
It's actually quite
similar to Wuling,

00:09:56.600 --> 00:09:57.000
where there are many people.

00:09:57.000 --> 00:09:59.666
Wuling. Wuling is a place to
chase snow and sunrises,

00:10:00.166 --> 00:10:02.666
and here's the Wuling Archway—that's
where everyone looks.

00:10:02.666 --> 00:10:03.700
We're here to see the
sunrise at Qilai (??).

00:10:05.233 --> 00:10:06.366
We shouldn't eat
such terrible food.

00:10:06.366 --> 00:10:09.900
And we have extra eggs,

00:10:09.900 --> 00:10:11.300
so it's only 15,
000 Indonesian Rupiah.

00:10:17.200 --> 00:10:18.600
Eating instant noodles
on the mountain

00:10:25.200 --> 00:10:26.300
is so satisfying! It
only costs 30 NTD.

00:10:26.800 --> 00:10:28.600
At an altitude of 2,

00:10:31.133 --> 00:10:32.800
400 meters, the sunrise occurred
while eating instant noodles.

00:10:37.766 --> 00:10:38.700
It wasn't too cold because
of the altitude of 2,

00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:42.433
400 meters, so I felt okay.
I wore [something] today.

00:10:43.266 --> 00:10:46.766
A wool base layer followed by a static mid
-layer vest

00:10:47.566 --> 00:10:49.900
Add a Kawas lightest down jacket

00:10:49.900 --> 00:10:51.133
and a GORE
-TEX shirt.

00:10:53.166 --> 00:10:55.333
The feeling of sunrise amidst

00:11:02.966 --> 00:11:04.600
the sea of clouds

00:11:12.500 --> 00:11:14.800
This place has a kind of ink painting

00:11:16.466 --> 00:11:18.000
feel to it (it's amazing!!)

00:11:25.033 --> 00:11:30.733
What is the smoke? Is it from a volcano? (Yes,
it's from a volcano!) Volcanic ash.

00:11:38.000 --> 00:11:41.200
The volcano behind it is
erupting and exploding!

00:11:44.100 --> 00:11:45.900
(Volcanic smoke keeps
billowing out!) Saying

00:11:53.866 --> 00:11:57.500
goodbye to Bromo volcano
was really awesome!

00:11:57.500 --> 00:12:00.900
It sprayed out,
it ejaculated! But now it's stopped.

00:12:02.800 --> 00:12:06.433
Let me repeat that here,
behind us is Semeru.

00:12:06.433 --> 00:12:10.800
Ahead is Kerilo (Batók volcano),
and this is where it's erupting.

00:12:10.800 --> 00:12:13.533
Bromo keeps spewing.

00:12:13.533 --> 00:12:16.900
We should be at the bottom
of the volcano soon.

00:12:17.033 --> 00:12:21.233
The photo was taken from the same spot where my feet were,
both when I was riding a Jeep there and now.

00:12:21.233 --> 00:12:24.433
The people had mostly dispersed,
and the atmosphere had become quite warm.

00:12:24.533 --> 00:12:27.933
If you come by yourself, you must hire a car,
so this time I'm going with...

00:12:29.466 --> 00:12:32.900
The tour itinerary for chartered cars
is different from what we used to do.

00:12:32.900 --> 00:12:36.166
I want to do it myself (as a backpacker),
but it's just too inconvenient.

00:12:36.233 --> 00:12:38.200
We traveled from Saiwu
Falls yesterday

00:12:38.200 --> 00:12:40.466
to Mount Bromo today.

00:12:40.466 --> 00:12:43.100
Now, we need to hire a Jeep to go to

00:12:43.566 --> 00:12:45.533
the crater of Mount Ijen tomorrow.

00:12:45.533 --> 00:12:48.500
The itinerary was specially arranged
because this place was just here.

00:12:48.500 --> 00:12:53.300
I asked the guide and he said there
are absolutely no public buses.

00:12:53.300 --> 00:12:56.166
There should usually be small towns where
you can hitch a ride up to Bromo,

00:12:56.166 --> 00:12:58.733
but...

00:12:58.733 --> 00:13:01.433
Without this,

00:13:01.433 --> 00:13:04.166
there was no Saiwu Falls yesterday,
no bus, no public transport.

00:13:04.166 --> 00:13:07.266
We need to hire a car,
so we went with a travel agency.

00:13:07.266 --> 00:13:10.033
It's very convenient to travel

00:13:10.033 --> 00:13:10.966
with wilderness travelers, OK?

00:13:10.966 --> 00:13:13.100
Now I'm going to Wuling
Archway to catch a Jeep

00:13:15.233 --> 00:13:16.833
(haha (the ink painting
is really beautiful)).

00:13:21.433 --> 00:13:24.633
You can see Bromo is yelling
at us as we walk

00:13:26.466 --> 00:13:29.100
down from the South Lake
Vegetable Garden (?).

00:13:38.333 --> 00:13:42.133
I don't know where it is,
but it's probably one by one.

00:13:42.133 --> 00:13:43.766
Hiss... Oh wow,

00:13:44.166 --> 00:13:46.033
that sounds like a sound effect! (It's
real! It's not a sound effect.)

00:13:47.066 --> 00:13:48.333
Are we going to take
this horse? To the

00:13:48.366 --> 00:13:51.166
volcano? I'm not sure either.

00:13:51.166 --> 00:13:52.700
Anyway, we're in a very
desolate place now.

00:13:53.566 --> 00:13:55.100
Then all of them were Jeep cars,

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:55.900
it looked like a movie scene.

00:13:57.666 --> 00:13:59.433
The one with lots of special effects
(I'm talking about Mad Max!).

00:14:01.200 --> 00:14:02.066
They will lead you by the horse,

00:14:02.800 --> 00:14:05.233
and then this...

00:14:05.366 --> 00:14:06.166
(Can't we add more whips? ~~~)

00:14:07.000 --> 00:14:08.333
Adding whips costs extra xddd

00:14:12.933 --> 00:14:14.066
I almost got a cramp
(I was terrified).

00:14:15.066 --> 00:14:18.866
I was so nervous I thought
I was going to fall.

00:14:21.466 --> 00:14:22.133
This core core

00:14:22.133 --> 00:14:23.600
eruption

00:14:24.733 --> 00:14:26.600
You just need to put on the
front half of the shoe.

00:14:27.433 --> 00:14:29.266
Because you need to be
ready to pull yourself

00:14:29.266 --> 00:14:31.700
out at any time when you're
about to fall.

00:14:31.700 --> 00:14:33.833
Just like with carding shoes! Just

00:14:33.833 --> 00:14:36.333
place the card where you want it.

00:14:40.500 --> 00:14:42.000
Is riding on horseback good? My

00:14:42.633 --> 00:14:43.900
brother is giving me a ride.

00:14:43.900 --> 00:14:45.100
I was also born in the
Year of the Horse,

00:14:47.900 --> 00:14:48.466
and he is now...

00:14:48.466 --> 00:14:50.633
I've never ridden a horse before,

00:14:51.600 --> 00:14:54.733
even at a 7/10 pace.

00:14:59.333 --> 00:15:01.166
Bro~~~ Brother Ma,

00:15:02.333 --> 00:15:04.200
don't go astray (A real horse
expert!!! So handsome!)

00:15:08.400 --> 00:15:10.200
(Princess Pearl rode away~~)
It sways up and down so

00:15:15.833 --> 00:15:18.633
you won't fall off;
you can't resist it.

00:15:18.633 --> 00:15:20.133
You need to go back
and use its force to

00:15:20.133 --> 00:15:22.133
your advantage and deflect its force.

00:15:23.933 --> 00:15:25.300
As someone born in the
Year of the Horse,

00:15:25.300 --> 00:15:29.400
that's all I can say about my feelings,
nothing more xd

00:15:29.400 --> 00:15:30.433
Even those born in the Year
of the Horse don't

00:15:30.433 --> 00:15:31.600
understand horses~ This is quite a...

00:15:31.600 --> 00:15:32.300
Fun experiences including Princess

00:15:32.300 --> 00:15:33.400
Pig on the grassland

00:15:33.400 --> 00:15:36.133
Riding on the grasslands
for a long time,

00:15:36.133 --> 00:15:39.700
the kickstand still hurts a bit,
even though it seems like I was in Jordan.

00:15:39.700 --> 00:15:42.133
They were supposed to
let us ride camels,

00:15:42.133 --> 00:15:44.566
but I didn't. I just played around with them
for a bit and didn't ride any camels.

00:15:44.566 --> 00:15:47.866
You are not a horse, so why do you think
a horse is tired? (An ancient saying?)

00:15:48.566 --> 00:15:50.266
The horse is currently
training for "King

00:15:51.733 --> 00:15:52.200
of the Mountains"!
Charging upwards!

00:15:58.400 --> 00:16:00.333
This is also a hiking trip,

00:16:00.333 --> 00:16:04.733
but the sand here is just sand,
nothing special.

00:16:04.733 --> 00:16:06.500
There are stairs,

00:16:18.533 --> 00:16:20.333
but wait a moment (to reach
the horse parking area).

00:16:29.866 --> 00:16:31.300
We're going up here now.

00:16:31.300 --> 00:16:33.800
Keliro's name is too hard to pronounce
(so the guides all pronounce it Keliro).

00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:35.200
It's called the Bromo

00:16:36.633 --> 00:16:37.966
Crater of Mount Krelu.

00:16:37.966 --> 00:16:40.466
Because you see it's
relatively short here,

00:16:40.466 --> 00:16:43.033
but it should be quite large.
You can see the jets of air above.

00:16:43.033 --> 00:16:44.066
The entire landscape is a spectacular

00:16:44.066 --> 00:16:47.200
volcanic formation.

00:16:48.233 --> 00:16:50.300
The tour guide said the most
difficult part of today's

00:16:50.300 --> 00:16:53.366
hike was the approximately 200
-250 steps.

00:16:54.633 --> 00:16:55.966
It's like building a staircase
on this volcanic terrain,

00:16:55.966 --> 00:16:59.133
so you can...

00:16:59.133 --> 00:17:02.733
I don't know why I was so short of
breath when I got to the crater today.

00:17:04.166 --> 00:17:06.266
We're heading towards
the volcano now,

00:17:10.100 --> 00:17:11.200
it seems like the Taipei
101 climbing race.

00:17:11.233 --> 00:17:13.000
This is roughly equivalent
to the panting

00:17:13.833 --> 00:17:14.733
level after climbing
about ten floors xd

00:17:26.233 --> 00:17:27.266
(Super spectacular!!) An active
volcano that keeps erupting,

00:17:27.266 --> 00:17:30.700
and then...

00:17:30.700 --> 00:17:33.666
What you see here is actually quite
spectacular; theoretically,

00:17:36.200 --> 00:17:39.566
you could walk around it like this.

00:17:39.566 --> 00:17:42.200
Theoretically, it seems possible to go
there because this won't lead to...

00:17:42.200 --> 00:17:45.066
The road surface is too steep,
but it's walkable.

00:17:45.066 --> 00:17:46.600
So most tourists come
up the stairs here and

00:17:46.600 --> 00:17:50.200
see this thing that's
been erupting.

00:17:50.200 --> 00:17:51.866
Its visibility must be like
this: it keeps spraying,

00:17:51.866 --> 00:17:56.333
and the smoke keeps rising,
so everything looks foggy.

00:17:57.000 --> 00:17:58.200
It's probably volcanic ash.
Did you see any other clouds? They're cold.

00:18:00.166 --> 00:18:01.666
When you see other clouds,

00:18:01.666 --> 00:18:04.766
the cold air will come
down to this location.

00:18:04.766 --> 00:18:06.566
It's spraying like crazy
over there!! There's

00:18:06.566 --> 00:18:08.100
nothing else to describe it.
.. it's just spraying!

00:18:15.200 --> 00:18:17.333
It's quite surprising that it
doesn't have much of a smell;

00:18:17.333 --> 00:18:20.066
I thought it would have a strong,
very unpleasant odor.

00:18:20.066 --> 00:18:21.033
But actually,

00:18:21.400 --> 00:18:22.700
it's okay that the
horse smells bad (XD)

00:18:33.300 --> 00:18:36.300
(Here) 4000 meters and then it collapsed.
After it collapsed...

00:18:36.300 --> 00:18:39.533
These small volcanoes have started
erupting again, so...

00:18:39.533 --> 00:18:41.666
They say it formed the volcano
within a volcano,

00:19:06.233 --> 00:19:08.033
Mount Muteleb.

00:19:11.500 --> 00:19:13.466
The riding instructors around
the volcano's

00:19:19.400 --> 00:19:22.300
edge were covered in horse hair.

00:19:22.866 --> 00:19:24.633
Some people are allergic
to horsehair,

00:19:25.000 --> 00:19:26.566
it's true! And it's not
just in Indonesian oil pits.

00:19:26.733 --> 00:19:28.366
It's still the Indonesian
Moon World~ This place

00:19:28.700 --> 00:19:30.366
is very similar to Moon World,
but because...

00:19:30.366 --> 00:19:32.100
The wilderness guide said
that this area is a very,

00:19:32.100 --> 00:19:33.800
very large volcano.

00:19:33.800 --> 00:19:35.333
As I just mentioned,
this place was originally a

00:19:35.333 --> 00:19:37.000
What happened after the volcano,

00:19:37.000 --> 00:19:38.966
with a diameter of ten kilometers and a height of over four kilometers,
finally collapsed?

00:19:38.966 --> 00:19:40.866
It's amazing that these
small volcanoes have grown.

00:19:40.866 --> 00:19:43.166
So originally,

00:19:43.166 --> 00:19:45.833
the entire volcanic cluster was like this;
these are what we would call ruins.

00:19:45.833 --> 00:19:48.966
It wasn't something washed
down by lava; rather,

00:19:48.966 --> 00:19:50.633
it was simply that the
terrain collapsed.

00:19:50.633 --> 00:19:53.100
So this is what it looks like now.

00:19:53.100 --> 00:19:56.800
There's actually an outer layer,

00:19:56.800 --> 00:19:59.200
which is the outer perimeter of the volcano.
We're at the observation deck.

00:19:59.200 --> 00:20:00.733
So we are now in that place.

00:20:00.733 --> 00:20:04.266
Let's go inside the volcano
to see this volcanic

00:20:04.266 --> 00:20:06.400
complex and take a
selfie with myself.

00:20:06.400 --> 00:20:08.266
Tourists and locals are about equal,

00:20:08.266 --> 00:20:09.966
so the locals

00:20:09.966 --> 00:20:11.833
We'll also visit this place
to conclude today's

00:20:11.833 --> 00:20:14.900
itinerary before heading
to Mount Ijen.

00:20:14.900 --> 00:20:16.366
Surabaya, which is near
the city I most want to

00:20:16.366 --> 00:20:17.933
visit, is the so
-called Surabaya in Indonesia.

00:20:17.933 --> 00:20:18.533
Blue Volcano Fried

00:20:20.766 --> 00:20:21.066
Chicken (???)

00:20:26.800 --> 00:20:28.866
(Me? Am I really that good at

00:20:28.866 --> 00:20:29.700
mountain climbing?) They...

00:20:31.733 --> 00:20:33.566
We're getting fried chicken soon!

00:20:34.766 --> 00:20:35.800
XDDD Because of the fried chicken!

00:20:35.800 --> 00:20:39.200
(Someone's going to pick

00:20:39.200 --> 00:20:40.200
this up later) Me???

00:20:40.200 --> 00:20:43.700
Thankfully, my chicken is still here;
I've already put it away.

00:20:44.066 --> 00:20:45.733
Where is it located? Do we need

00:20:46.233 --> 00:20:47.000
to send a higher
-level vehicle?

00:20:47.000 --> 00:20:50.000
Of the 99 peaks (100 mountains) at a high level,
I can only rank second.

00:20:50.000 --> 00:20:52.966
99 went to pick it up
(99 went?) (Anyway,

00:20:54.200 --> 00:20:57.900
I came in the end...)

00:20:59.466 --> 00:21:02.300
Our photographer disappeared
after climbing up.

00:21:04.033 --> 00:21:09.200
(We met some locals who offered
to take us to collect them.)

00:21:12.766 --> 00:21:16.966
This is something I noticed
when I used my phone

00:21:16.966 --> 00:21:20.200
to zoom in; it's a four
-cornered device.

00:21:21.500 --> 00:21:22.633
It really was that far (and

00:21:26.133 --> 00:21:27.466
we actually found it!).

00:21:28.833 --> 00:21:29.666
This is surprisingly accurate (I

00:21:33.266 --> 00:21:35.333
got this view unexpectedly).

00:21:39.000 --> 00:21:41.966
Now, after retrieving the drone,
I unexpectedly

00:21:43.333 --> 00:21:44.800
saw a magnificent view.

00:21:45.833 --> 00:21:47.766
Everything over there is white,

00:21:47.766 --> 00:21:48.400
like it's snowing.

00:21:51.100 --> 00:21:53.966
Our dogs don't need
to walk by themselves.

00:21:54.000 --> 00:21:55.333
Our dog's name is Ma
Zou XDDDD Slow down,

00:21:56.666 --> 00:21:58.100
slow down (please him first).

00:22:04.633 --> 00:22:06.433
Remember to touch this side after you
dismount; it will make him happy.

00:22:07.133 --> 00:22:09.100
Thank you. Bye
-bye.

00:22:17.733 --> 00:22:20.066
(Upon reaching an open area in the distance,
one can see the entire Keliro volcano.)

00:22:21.533 --> 00:22:24.300
(Bromo continued to emit smoke) (This

00:22:26.300 --> 00:22:28.066
is not a prohibited scene...)

00:22:33.133 --> 00:22:37.400
It's right at the
entrance; you can

00:22:43.266 --> 00:22:45.300
see the volcano directly
and eat there.

00:22:54.166 --> 00:22:56.133
(Somewhat like the fu in
Taitung) (Passing by the

00:23:03.400 --> 00:23:05.533
largest thermal power
plant on Java Island)

00:23:06.600 --> 00:23:09.066
Everyone, I woke up with my hair
sticking up and I was furious!

00:23:09.066 --> 00:23:12.800
We've arrived at our
hotel around 3 PM now,

00:23:12.800 --> 00:23:18.766
which is completely baffling.

00:23:18.766 --> 00:23:21.066
Having a swimming pool is ridiculous
because we have to

00:23:21.066 --> 00:23:23.300
go to Ijen Volcano very early tomorrow,
so today is...

00:23:23.300 --> 00:23:26.500
We've reached a place close to Ijin,
but haven't arrived yet.

00:23:26.500 --> 00:23:29.166
Because if they were to stay all
the way to the third floor today,

00:23:29.166 --> 00:23:30.766
it would be too far, Bromo.

00:23:30.766 --> 00:23:32.566
So, it's at a midpoint with Yi
-jin, therefore

00:23:32.566 --> 00:23:34.633
I have to leave very early tomorrow,

00:23:34.633 --> 00:23:36.900
at 12 o'clock, to continue my journey by bus.
I didn't actually take any pictures to show you.

00:23:36.900 --> 00:23:38.733
Most of the time was spent hitchhiking
because of Indonesia.

00:23:38.733 --> 00:23:40.100
This is really huge,

00:23:41.033 --> 00:23:42.066
Java!

00:23:49.333 --> 00:23:51.000
I should go to bed early
tonight because

00:23:51.000 --> 00:23:53.700
I have to get up again at midnight.

00:23:54.333 --> 00:23:56.233
(I find it absurd) But

00:23:56.266 --> 00:23:57.200
that's how it is.

00:23:57.200 --> 00:24:00.900
ROOM TOUR!

00:24:03.800 --> 00:24:05.333
It's nice,

00:24:05.333 --> 00:24:08.933
small and beautiful, and clean.
I'm not sure if it should be considered one.

00:24:08.933 --> 00:24:11.700
It's a third
-tier city,

00:24:11.700 --> 00:24:13.900
a small settlement,
not really a city, just a small settlement.

00:24:13.900 --> 00:24:15.733
The feel of Taitung? We're
looking forward to tomorrow!

00:24:15.733 --> 00:24:18.100
The blue flames of Ijen Volcano,

00:24:18.100 --> 00:24:20.933
the dog dragging your luggage
at 11:30 tonight.

00:24:20.933 --> 00:24:24.000
Li Xiang, check out here.

00:24:24.000 --> 00:24:26.666
OK. The most important thing for this trip
is this sports protection capsule.

00:24:26.700 --> 00:24:28.733
A slight illness followed
by overwork can

00:24:28.733 --> 00:24:31.633
help improve one's
physical condition.

00:24:31.633 --> 00:24:33.933
Magnesium is also important; I take
magnesium capsules after dinner.

00:24:36.600 --> 00:24:42.300
What do you think of this
very special salty cookie?

00:24:42.300 --> 00:24:44.300
Taiwanese people do have this kind of pancake
(it's a very sweet pancake!).

00:24:44.733 --> 00:24:47.100
Too sweet, too sweet.

00:24:47.100 --> 00:24:51.900
.. (Let's have dinner at the restaurant
downstairs in the hotel)

00:24:52.066 --> 00:24:55.933
Hokkien fried noodles cost NT$35, which is roughly a serving for 2
-3 people...

00:24:55.933 --> 00:24:59.500
(The four men ordered an enormous
amount of food...)

00:24:59.500 --> 00:25:05.766
(Beef steak, steamed dumplings,
steamed buns, roast duck, oxtail soup)

00:25:05.766 --> 00:25:09.500
The fried noodles were delicious,
and so was the oxtail soup.

00:25:12.133 --> 00:25:16.300
Pizza Hut is getting ready to
go to sleep because I can only

00:25:16.300 --> 00:25:19.666
sleep for four hours,
and there are some things outside.

00:25:19.666 --> 00:25:23.200
We were very full from the Indonesian street
food and then prepared to go back.

00:25:23.200 --> 00:25:24.266
Pack up and go to sleep

00:25:24.266 --> 00:25:27.300
at 11:30 PM!! (Get up!)

00:25:29.366 --> 00:25:31.600
Good morning everyone.

00:25:31.600 --> 00:25:34.100
We're at the trailhead in Ijen now because
we're starting our ascent at 2 PM.

00:25:34.100 --> 00:25:36.733
The control station doesn't
depart until 2 PM,

00:25:36.733 --> 00:25:39.600
so we're preparing
to depart at 1:55 AM.

00:25:39.600 --> 00:25:41.900
In Indonesia,

00:25:41.900 --> 00:25:46.400
most people invest 5,000 rupiah,
so you should prepare some 5,000 rupiah banknotes.

00:25:46.400 --> 00:25:49.433
We are currently at an altitude
of around 1900 meters,

00:25:49.433 --> 00:25:53.100
and we plan to climb to 2400 meters.

00:25:53.100 --> 00:25:55.566
The ascent is over 500 meters and 3.

00:25:56.000 --> 00:25:58.800
7 kilometers; it says that's
a normal walking distance.

00:25:58.800 --> 00:26:02.066
It takes about an hour and a half to walk slowly,
or if you walk fast...

00:26:02.066 --> 00:26:04.566
It might only take an hour
to climb Mount Ijen.

00:26:04.566 --> 00:26:07.300
The so
-called blue flame is one of only

00:26:07.300 --> 00:26:10.866
two visible blue flames in the world.

00:26:10.866 --> 00:26:13.566
One place is in Iceland,
and the other is in

00:26:13.566 --> 00:26:15.600
The Ijen volcano in
Indonesia has been

00:26:15.600 --> 00:26:16.600
talked about as a blue volcano...

00:26:16.600 --> 00:26:19.900
Actually, it should be called Blue Flame,
the blue flame

00:26:19.900 --> 00:26:22.066
they call it,
which comes from this Ijen volcano.

00:26:22.066 --> 00:26:24.700
One of the volcanic
lakes formed inside

00:26:24.700 --> 00:26:27.133
The guide will introduce the
blue flame to us later.

00:26:27.133 --> 00:26:30.266
We really didn't do our research,
but it was...

00:26:30.266 --> 00:26:32.966
I've known about this blue volcano for a very,
very long time.

00:26:32.966 --> 00:26:35.733
I didn't know the blue
-flaming

00:26:35.733 --> 00:26:37.866
volcano was called Mount Ijin.

00:26:37.866 --> 00:26:39.966
The location is really very
close to Bali; it's

00:26:39.966 --> 00:26:42.466
actually a 45
-minute boat ride to Bali on the right.

00:26:42.466 --> 00:26:44.600
So if you want to visit Bali,

00:26:44.600 --> 00:26:47.266
you can take a boat from here
and then go a little further.

00:26:47.266 --> 00:26:49.100
You can go to Lombok and climb

00:26:49.100 --> 00:26:51.500
a place called Mount Agung.

00:26:51.500 --> 00:26:54.166
Join a volcano traverse
in Indonesia! (Remember

00:26:56.033 --> 00:26:59.200
to bring a gas mask as the
air will be pungent.)

00:27:03.300 --> 00:27:04.533
It looks like we're going to play Counter
-Strike (what a brat xd).

00:27:11.766 --> 00:27:14.666
Guide: We should mainly follow their
(the local guides') instructions.

00:27:15.833 --> 00:27:17.233
Let's take a group photo here

00:27:34.600 --> 00:27:37.133
in Lamborghinis!!! (Locals say)

00:27:38.810 --> 00:27:42.600
If you don't want to leave,
you can take this bulldozer that was converted.

00:27:42.600 --> 00:27:45.966
A rickshaw (or pedicab?)
(A companion needed a

00:27:45.966 --> 00:27:48.600
ride for filming!) We're
really off now!

00:27:53.033 --> 00:27:55.966
(Two people pull from the front and push from the back,
an old man pushing a cart)

00:27:57.566 --> 00:27:59.166
Rickshaws take up a lot of road space

00:28:05.766 --> 00:28:07.666
(the Empress Dowager has arrived!).

00:28:19.006 --> 00:28:20.700
Awesome! Awesome! Awesome!
(Laughs so hard,

00:28:20.700 --> 00:28:22.142
the Chinese are really
good at teaching!)

00:28:22.900 --> 00:28:26.633
bugatti bugatti bugatti oh~ (When
did it change to bugatti?)

00:28:27.766 --> 00:28:30.666
Whatever kind of vehicle you need,
and what brand it is, we have it here!

00:28:34.541 --> 00:28:35.800
It was quite steep (everyone took

00:28:37.566 --> 00:28:40.366
off their coats except me).

00:28:42.900 --> 00:28:44.966
This is seriously something
I could sleep

00:28:44.966 --> 00:28:47.503
in; I want to sleep
away all my shame!!

00:28:54.400 --> 00:28:56.633
There were seven rest stops in total,

00:29:19.266 --> 00:29:22.561
and it was very chaotic because
there were just too many people.

00:29:22.599 --> 00:29:24.833
So what I was originally going to
say was that this is very similar

00:29:24.833 --> 00:29:27.500
to some kind of Hundred Peaks route,
it should be like...

00:29:27.500 --> 00:29:28.533
I can't tell you the

00:29:28.533 --> 00:29:29.566
route to Xiangshan.

00:29:29.566 --> 00:29:34.000
So many people climbed 300 meters,
so it's only 200 meters more and we'll get there.

00:29:39.835 --> 00:29:41.266
(Met Celine's fans!) Okay,

00:29:43.000 --> 00:29:46.800
I've never been here before.

00:29:46.800 --> 00:29:48.700
Bali feels a lot like climbing a

00:29:56.391 --> 00:29:58.540
mountain in the dark in Taiwan.

00:05:07.533 --> 00:05:10.733
Down...down...(Taking a bath)

00:06:06.566 --> 00:06:08.233
Pineapple Custard Apple

00:06:51.700 --> 00:06:52.700
It's so steep! (Guide: Remember

00:10:29.500 --> 00:10:30.833
to stir it!!!) (So thoughtful!)

00:20:25.333 --> 00:20:26.766
That guy who's really good at

00:24:34.333 --> 00:24:36.400
hiking? (Found some weird snacks)

00:27:01.304 --> 00:27:02.766
(A bit funny.

00:27:10.127 --> 00:27:11.133
..) Filtering toxic gas

00:27:26.452 --> 00:27:28.252
(There are a lot of people,
so remember to stick with your guide.)

00:28:09.388 --> 00:28:10.851
She also wants to ride

00:28:14.669 --> 00:28:16.433
in a Lamborghini!

00:28:46.748 --> 00:28:47.471
(Laughing so hard) We've

00:30:06.966 --> 00:30:10.833
now arrived at Hehuan North!

00:30:10.903 --> 00:30:13.833
Hehuan North Peak is their
Lamborghini parking lot.

00:30:13.833 --> 00:30:15.833
The main place is the Snow
Lord's Emerald Pool.

00:30:18.966 --> 00:30:21.520
(Cut down from the mountaintop to the
volcanic lake to see the blue flames)

00:30:29.462 --> 00:30:32.233
The road down is quite narrow,
so there are oncoming vehicles passing each other.

00:30:35.233 --> 00:30:37.799
Sulfur Ore (Arrives

00:30:40.495 --> 00:30:41.833
at Blue Flame)

00:31:19.624 --> 00:31:21.425
(The flames will drip down,
so don't get too close.)

00:31:25.766 --> 00:31:29.200
People were taking pictures
with this dying flame.

00:31:29.766 --> 00:31:35.757
I was so touched (I just couldn't
stop crying).

00:31:39.500 --> 00:31:42.166
(After watching the return journey) I

00:31:46.233 --> 00:31:49.000
saw miners going up
and down the mine.

00:31:52.933 --> 00:31:56.666
I can't take it back (because it's flammable
and can't be taken on the plane).

00:32:04.933 --> 00:32:06.266
Back on the ridgeline,

00:32:12.166 --> 00:32:15.766
the volcanic lake is much
larger than expected.

00:32:15.766 --> 00:32:19.533
So now there's smoke
with sulfur in it,

00:32:19.533 --> 00:32:21.466
which is a dream come true, right?

00:32:25.720 --> 00:32:28.387
(Looking at the blue flame from
where the smoke was just now)

00:32:30.600 --> 00:32:31.866
New Kangshan (it looks like the
New Kangtian Palace Fortress)

00:32:43.466 --> 00:32:46.933
Everyone gathers here
to watch the sunrise.

00:32:46.933 --> 00:32:49.466
It's said that this is the
real triangle spot of Yizhen,

00:32:52.899 --> 00:32:55.266
and you can still smell a
faint sulfurous odor here.

00:32:55.299 --> 00:32:58.133
Quite a few people still

00:32:58.133 --> 00:33:00.300
wear that mask.

00:33:18.533 --> 00:33:20.966
The summit is over 2700 meters
high; the triangulation

00:33:20.966 --> 00:33:22.933
point should be at this location now.

00:33:22.933 --> 00:33:24.833
The location is around 2300 meters,

00:33:24.833 --> 00:33:26.900
but nobody climbs it because it's
not one of the Hundred Peaks.

00:33:26.900 --> 00:33:29.433
Is it good or bad? Because I think this
place looks a lot like Jiaming Lake.

00:33:29.433 --> 00:33:31.566
Sancha Mountain,

00:33:31.566 --> 00:33:33.933
but because Sancha Mountain is one of the Hundred Peaks,
nobody goes there.

00:33:33.933 --> 00:33:36.466
They said there was nothing you could do if you climbed to the top,
so nobody went.

00:33:36.466 --> 00:33:40.466
Everyone's taking pictures of
Ijen's volcanic lake; the

00:33:41.133 --> 00:33:43.233
volcanic lake is incredibly,
incredibly, incredibly blue.

00:33:43.233 --> 00:33:47.066
As you can see,
this area is completely blue.

00:33:47.891 --> 00:33:51.366
That's because sulfur reacts
with heat to produce...

00:33:51.517 --> 00:33:55.533
Some high temperatures seem to indicate
that the temperature is

00:33:55.533 --> 00:33:58.233
high enough, because not all volcanoes
have high temperatures.

00:33:58.233 --> 00:34:00.466
Such a high flame requires
a very high temperature,

00:34:00.466 --> 00:34:04.033
but just the right amount of heat is
obviously not noticeable to the body.

00:34:04.033 --> 00:34:05.700
We can't feel how high
the temperature is.

00:34:05.700 --> 00:34:07.433
They could get very close
to the blue flame,

00:34:07.433 --> 00:34:11.300
but their previous experience
was relatively...

00:34:11.300 --> 00:34:13.933
When it's at its most vigorous,
you can see the whole area.

00:34:13.933 --> 00:34:15.166
The blue flame (slip of the tongue)

00:34:15.166 --> 00:34:17.266
That trickle of little blue flame

00:34:17.266 --> 00:34:18.800
A small piece on top and then
a small piece below, and

00:34:18.800 --> 00:34:20.966
It's actually quite dangerous; you can't
get too close because of that...

00:34:20.966 --> 00:34:23.433
The fire was probably quite hot,

00:34:23.433 --> 00:34:25.866
and during filming, some falling rocks
(from the flames) also came down.

00:34:25.866 --> 00:34:29.033
The bottom is the same hole
as the small oil pit.

00:34:29.033 --> 00:34:30.466
These traces left by the sulfurous

00:34:30.466 --> 00:34:33.300
(mountain walls) volcano

00:34:33.300 --> 00:34:35.466
So the filming experience is actually
a bit similar to the Hundred

00:34:35.466 --> 00:34:37.333
Peaks of Taiwan.
We just talked to the guide about this.

00:34:37.333 --> 00:34:39.566
In other words, we all think the mountains
in Taiwan are very beautiful.

00:34:39.566 --> 00:34:41.466
It's a pity that tourism
hasn't developed,

00:34:41.466 --> 00:34:44.133
but I think it's unlikely because
we've been talking about...

00:34:44.133 --> 00:34:47.133
This kind of culture allows people to go up
the mountain without restrictions; there

00:34:47.133 --> 00:34:49.533
are even rickshaws available to transport
people to the first mountain in Taiwan.

00:34:49.533 --> 00:34:51.766
It's impossible to pull a rickshaw
to the second altitude.

00:34:51.766 --> 00:34:54.533
If you are really assuming the relationship
is based on Jiaming Lake

00:34:54.533 --> 00:34:57.133
I certainly think that route
should be open for tourism.

00:34:57.133 --> 00:34:58.800
The point is not a problem, but

00:34:58.800 --> 00:35:00.466
Because the altitude is so high,

00:35:00.466 --> 00:35:03.666
3300 meters, mountains are extremely prone to altitude sickness,
and the rescue efforts alone are a huge challenge.

00:35:03.666 --> 00:35:05.566
It's possible that a bunch
of people will be carried off

00:35:05.566 --> 00:35:07.033
the road along the way,
so don't talk about it going up.

00:35:07.033 --> 00:35:09.433
A bunch of people were carried down,
so the mountains in Taiwan are still...

00:35:09.433 --> 00:35:11.425
It's difficult to develop on a large
scale; the mountain roads are constantly

00:35:11.533 --> 00:35:14.333
